<div class="prose">
  <h1>About Repverse</h1>
  <span class="updated">The Stacks ecosystem, made explorable.</span>

  <p>
    Repverse is an explorer built for the Stacks (STX) ecosystem. It brings together BNS names,
    NFT collections, token holdings, stacking rewards, and transaction history into one place —
    so you can look up a wallet by its address or its BNS name and get the full picture instantly.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Resolve BNS names to addresses and back again</li>
    <li>View NFT collections and fungible token balances for any wallet</li>
    <li>Estimate stacking rewards with the stake calculator</li>
    <li>Browse full, paginated transaction history</li>
    <li>Compare two wallets or BNS names side by side</li>
    <li>Convert STX and other assets to fiat or crypto in real time</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Repverse reads public chain data from the Stacks blockchain API and BNS registry. Nothing you
    look up is private — it's the same data available on any public Stacks explorer, just organized
    around the wallet rather than the block.
  </p>

  <h2>Sign in, if you want to</h2>
  <p>
    You can use Repverse without an account. Signing in with Google or connecting a Stacks wallet
    just lets you save wallets to a personal watchlist and pick up where you left off.
  </p>
</div>
